      "body": "## Credited prior result, not new mathematics\nRow 1910 / 30002271 / OWR-12330-013: already_solved1, one completed prior-proof audit (Turns 1/5). Andrew D. King, joint work with Katherine Edwards, explicitly supplies the clique-plus-pendants example in “Getting to the point of Reed’s Conjecture: How local can you go?”, Oberwolfach Report 02/2013, pp.103–105. Original report: https://ems.press/journals/owr/articles/12330 ; official PDF: https://ems.press/content/serial-article-files/46434 . Edwards–King, “A superlocal version of Reed’s Conjecture”, section 6, confirms the calculation: https://arxiv.org/abs/1208.5188v2 .\n\nThe accepted scope is the exact existential unrounded closed-neighborhood-average question only. For k>=2 the construction has chi_f=k and average 3k/4+1, strictly separated exactly for k>=5. The k=1 exception, k=4 equality, and both neighborhood types are explicit. No novelty, absolute minimum-order claim, maximal-clique-average conjecture, outer-subgraph bound, or universal local-demand result is claimed. The all-k written proof is separate from finite checks.\n\n## Public package and queue\nNineteen byte-preserved files include authored exposition and audit, verification scripts, generated certificates, targeted regression tests, and public source metadata. No copied source documents/text, corpus/dataset contents, private sources, private receipts or coordination files are distributed. Original package statements that publication/queue edits were not performed describe historical preparation, not this PR.\n\nThe complete existing QUEUE is preserved except row1910 Status, Turns and Findings. All unrelated rows, existing notes and chat links remain byte-identical. No main write or merge is requested.\n\nThis AI-assisted, unrefereed scoped audit and artifact verification is not external human peer review, journal acceptance, or proof-assistant certification. Recorded source-byte evidence is not a fresh retrieval or exhaustive current-literature search.\n\n## Identity and verification\nBase: c3a281e6bb3161f9e03ec0b874f3fdfe29d7c93f.\nHead: 881dbe65a5f83cab5950c1e58ddb1bc4d3f7ea8d.\nPublic MANIFEST.json: 2,877 bytes, SHA-256 bc54c2731f962b0a5b26fd19c2d14bc26513f481e18aef2d1f5a96ae53fa15c6.\nExact-head byte readback, normal/optimized replay, and actual CI observations will be reported separately after verification; no CI pass is asserted here.",
